  "question": {
    "text": "Let the centre of a circle, passing through the points $(0,0),(1,0)$ and touching the circle $x^2+y^2=9$, be $(h, k)$. Then for all possible values of the coordinates of the centre $(h, k), 4\\left(h^2+k^2\\right)$ is equal to_________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/X6ZDAbgntZzldqdmtHoabAG8UD8Gk_ry9VnblQ3-Dac.original.fullsize.png\"><br />$\\begin{aligned} & (\\mathrm{x}-\\mathrm{h})^2+(\\mathrm{y}-\\mathrm{k})^2=\\mathrm{h}^2+\\mathrm{k}^2 \\\\ & \\mathrm{x}^2+\\mathrm{y}^2-2 \\mathrm{hx}-2 \\mathrm{ky}=0 \\\\ & \\because \\text { passes through }(1,0) \\\\ & \\Rightarrow 1+0-2 \\mathrm{~h}=0 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{h}=1 / 2 \\\\ & \\because \\mathrm{OC}=\\frac{\\mathrm{OP}}{2} \\\\ & \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2+\\mathrm{k}^2}=\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{1}{4}+\\mathrm{k}^2=\\frac{9}{4} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{k}^2=2 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{k}= \\pm \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\therefore$ Possible coordinate of\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{c}(\\mathrm{h}, \\mathrm{k})\\left(\\frac{1}{2}, \\sqrt{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{2},-\\sqrt{2}\\right) \\\\\n& 4\\left(\\mathrm{~h}^2+\\mathrm{k}^2\\right)=4\\left(\\frac{1}{4}+2\\right)=4\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)=9\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
